Package: simeq
Title: Simulation for Equity: Dynamic Microsimulation of BMI, Health and Economic Outcomes
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person(
        given = "Berta",
        family = "Valente",
        email = "berta.valente@ispup.up.pt",
        role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description: An individual-level, stochastic, open-cohort dynamic
    microsimulation of adult body mass index (BMI) trajectories and their
    health and economic consequences, stratified by sex and educational
    attainment. The package separates a reusable simulation engine from
    setting-specific inputs and provides functions for input preparation,
    population initialisation, percentile-specific synthetic-cohort BMI
    transitions estimated from repeated cross-sectional surveys, mortality with
    BMI and education relative risks, education transitions, entrant
    generation, outcome estimation (quality-adjusted life years, obesity-
    attributable QALY loss and years of life lost, and high-BMI- and
    obesity-attributable direct medical costs) and diagnostics. The Portuguese
    reference implementation (SIMEQ-PT) simulates adults aged 20-84 years from
    1998 to 2040.
